 "note": "Sparse keys, approved in the keys lab (round 3) and read by the app since liquid-space round 1 (`src/keys-phrase.ts`); place-neutral rows a place table admits. Mostly two chords, each struck once where it lands and left to ring into the space. `chords` play in turn, each for its `bars` (8 and 8 by default at 174 BPM, a 16-bar cycle; a row may say 4 and 4). `left` and `right` are the plain voicing as MIDI notes (the root low and alone or with a shell fifth or seventh; a rootless right hand, wide), `deep` the landing voicing a pickup sinks into (the left hand spread to root, fifth and tenth or a low octave, the right a little lower or fuller), `scale` the pitch classes a motif over the chord draws from, `retouch` at most one quiet right-hand touch inside the chord's bars, `vel` a softer strike. `root` is the chord's root by name; the bed's sub reads `left[0]`. `fromProgressions` maps round 2's progressions to the nearest phrase, for his old links. `levelDb` is the keys' level on this writing, under the bed and with headroom for a strike in a wet space. In the app (revision 2) a theme draws one row by its `weight` among those whose notes fit its key (moved by the semitones that take its key root onto the theme's, or onto the degree that fits), the chords change only where the keys land, and each chord's `bass` is the bass line's home under it: `key` the row's key root held as a pedal (only where it is a tone of the chord), `root` the chord's own root. Chosen by measurement (liquid-space round 1, the round note has the table): the share of the liquid riffs' time (their bar shapes, by length) that lands on a tone of the chord over each home first — the riff is the line the bass plays for bars, and its minor shape over the tonic pedal sits on a VI chord's third, fifth and seventh — and where the two are within 0.02, the low register (`lowClash`: the chord's notes under E3 that beat with the home).",
